---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="Who am I?">
    <section class="mb-20">
        <h1 class="section-title text-4xl mb-2">About</h1>
        <p class="led-accent text-sm mb-12">// About me</p>

        <div class="max-w-3xl">
            <div class="card mb-8">
                <p class="t-muted leading-relaxed mb-6">
                    My name is Bruno Fonseca and I love building things and watch them work.<br/><br/>
                    I'm most experienced in Firmware and Embedded Software development.
                    <br/>
                    I have a background in Electrical Engineering and I love to build
                    things and watch them come to life.<br/>
                    <br/>
                    I also like to experiment with 3D printing, 3D design, hardware
                    and home automation.<br/>
                    In my free time I like to cook, explore nature and do some amateur photography now and then. <br/>
                    I love martial arts, video games and understanding how stuff works. <br/>
                    <br/>
                    Like any good engineer worth their salt, I love me a good coffe cup! <br/>
                    Just kidding, you don't have to drink coffe. Tea is also allowed 😉
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <p class="led-accent text-sm mb-12">// About DebugLED</p>
        <div class="max-w-3xl">
            <div class="card mb-8">
                <p class="t-muted leading-relaxed mb-6">
                    Why DebugLED?<br/>
                    Have you ever wondered what the most important component is on a PCB?<br/><br/>

                    Most would say the MCU, some would say the transistor, others a fuse.
                    To me it's that simple diode that lights up when nothing else works. The Debug LED.<br/><br/> 

                    If you've ever designed Hardware, you know what I'm talking about.<br/><br/>

                    The one single thing that you can rely on when nothing else is working. 
                    The one fundamental component that allows you to implement the more complex systems on the board. <br/>
                    Before SPI, before UART, before the display, before any other feedback system. <br/>
                    Sometimes, the only feedback system you have on the board. <br/>
                    The first thing you code when writting the firmware.<br/><br/> 

                    In those initial moments, it's the sole indicator that there's power, the MCU is working and processing 
                    your code and that, if all else fails, you'll have that one beacon of feedback from the hardware to 
                    debug your design and code.<br/><br/>

                    And that's why, to me, this single tiny diode is the most important component in any PCB!<br/><br/>

                    <em>PS: Ok, let's not forget the resistor, otherwise we just have a burned LED 😅</em>
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>



    </section>
</BaseLayout>